.TH LUCERNA 1 "@DATE@" "Lucerna @VERSION@" "Lucerna"
.SH NAME
lucerna \- graphical control application for Lucerna animated wallpapers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lucerna
.RB [ \-v | \-\-verbose ]
.br
.B lucerna
.RB ( \-\-help | \-\-version )
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lucerna
opens the Lucerna control window: the wallpaper library, the displays, the settings and an About
page. It never plays wallpapers itself; it talks to the background service
.BR lucernad (1)
over the session D-Bus, and starts the service if it is not running. Closing the window does not
stop the wallpaper.
.PP
A graphical session is required. Without one,
.B lucerna
prints an explanation and exits with status 1;
.B \-\-help
and
.B \-\-version
work anywhere.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log at debug level.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LUCERNA_LOG, RUST_LOG
Log filter, for example
.BR lucerna=debug .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/lucerna/config.toml
Configuration (written only by the service).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lucernad (1),
.BR lucernactl (1)
.PP
Full documentation is in /usr/share/doc/lucerna.
